      "writtenOn": "2022-05-24T17:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two concerns here:\n- future calling convention extensions\n- leaking information via register.\n\nThe former is the reason we require x1..x3 to be zero in Linux/arm64, as otherwise, we would never be able to make use of those registers as we would not be able to distinguish garbage from actual values.\n\nAs for leaking info: the payload executes at the same EL as the loader, and can observe its entire memory image, so I\u0027m not sure zeroing registers provides any safety.",
      "parentUuid": "3134e153_e82f1295",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
